References: <20061002210813.42737.qmail@web30805.mail.mud.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <20061002213254.258520@gmx.net>

Hi Tao,

using the x and the y coordinates in the annotation file, i.e., e.g., hgu133plus2probe$x and hgu133plus2probe$y, and the functions xy2indices and pmindex.

Let tmp be an Affybatch object, and NR the number of rows on the chip (for the Plus2 chip, NR=1,164). Then something like

> pI<-unlist(pmindex(tmp))
> mat.xy<-cbind(x=hgu133plus2probe$x,y=hgu133plus2probe$y)
> ids.probes<-xy2indices(mat.xy,nr=NR)
> match(ids.probes,pI)

should work.

Best,
Holger

