From naomi at stat.psu.edu  Fri Oct  6 17:25:48 2006
From: naomi at stat.psu.edu (Naomi Altman)
Date: Fri, 06 Oct 2006 11:25:48 -0400
Subject: [BioC] Separate Normalizations and expression plotting
In-Reply-To: <200610060657.25621.sdavis2@mail.nih.gov>
References: <003701c6e8e4$cf2a9620$54508389@menton>
	<200610060657.25621.sdavis2@mail.nih.gov>
Message-ID: <6.2.3.4.2.20061006112336.021157b8@imap.stat.psu.edu>

It is important to remember that statistical significance refers to 
the investigator's ability to reproduce the result.  A result can be 
statistically significant without having biological 
significance.  The reported R-sq might be statistically significant 
but biologically insignificant.

--Naomi

