From durincks at mail.nih.gov  Mon Oct 30 21:16:52 2006
From: durincks at mail.nih.gov (Steffen Durinck)
Date: Mon, 30 Oct 2006 15:16:52 -0500
Subject: [BioC] biomaRt: retrieve total chromosome lengths
In-Reply-To: <45424FB1.7030201@med.umich.edu>
References: <CAFCC77E2969C94FB27BA6A816EC33296AD5BB@janbebeexs2.eu.jnj.com>
	<45424FB1.7030201@med.umich.edu>
Message-ID: <45465DB4.6030003@mail.nih.gov>

Hi An,

There is no way to retrieve the chromosome lengths with biomaRt when 
used with Ensembl.
The closest you'll get with biomaRt is to subtract the position of the 
'first' transcript from the position of the 'last' transcript.

If you want to use the Ensembl data to get this information (you'll need 
to do some browser clicking), you can select your species of interest at
http://www.ensembl.org/

for hsapiens:

